From: Stel777 <274792865+Stel777@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 15:47:08 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] feat(source-folders): port the "Full import (code)"
 button onto v0.6.0
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Upstream's sync mirrors markdown only, and its new "Index code" reads code
STRUCTURE into the graph (native tree-sitter) without bringing the files
into the vault. Neither covers the /update-brain importer path, where every
file type is copied in and code/html/binary become `.neurovault.md`
sidecars, so recall can retrieve them as text.

project_import.rs needed no changes — the four memory APIs it depends on
(registry_source_folders, resolve_vault_path, ingest_file, SourceFolder)
all still exist in v0.6.0, so this is just wiring: the module declaration,
a POST /api/brains/:brain_id/sources/full_import route matching upstream's
sibling handlers, a brainStore call, and the button beside "Index code".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
